  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Who answers a request",
      "items": [
        "Unlisted route: API Gateway returns 404 {\"message\":\"Not Found\"}; Lambda never runs.",
        "Over 10 rps (burst 20): API Gateway returns 429 before invoking.",
        "Listed route: the Go handler switches on RouteKey and returns 200, 400 (bad /echo body) or its own 404.",
        "Crash or timeout (10 s): API Gateway returns 500."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Two directions of trust",
      "items": [
        "Who may CALL the function: the Lambda permission, principal apigateway.amazonaws.com, source_arn = this API's execution_arn/*/*.",
        "What the function may DO: its execution role trusts lambda.amazonaws.com and only has AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole (write logs)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Build, deploy, release",
      "items": [
        "terraform/bootstrap (local state) runs once and creates the lesson's own S3 state bucket via modules/state-bucket.",
        "GOOS=linux GOARCH=arm64 CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -tags lambda.norpc produces build/bootstrap.",
        "data.archive_file zips it with a fixed mode; the zip hash is the code version.",
        "terraform apply creates 12 resources the first time; after a rebuild it updates only the function code."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Scope of this drawing",
      "items": [
        "Drawn from the lesson13 Terraform and Go source; not a live AWS inventory.",
        "The dev root keeps state in S3 with S3-native locking (use_lockfile); the bucket is versioned, encrypted, HTTPS-only and protected by prevent_destroy."
      ]
    }
  ]
